= Start here =

BITwiki is a MediaWiki-based semantic knowledge and memory system. It is designed so public knowledge can be read normally, queried structurally, reused through transclusion, and improved without losing provenance.

== Start with these pages ==
* [[BITwiki:Manifesto]] — why BITwiki exists.
* [[BITwiki:Charter]] — mission and scope.
* [[BITwiki:Constitution]] — durable public invariants.
* [[BITwiki:Foundational triad]] — ontology, epistemology, and axiology.
* [[BITwiki:Architecture]] — system structure.
* [[BITwiki:Book matter]] — reusable semantic content anatomy.
* [[BITwiki:Epistemics]] — evidence, sources, uncertainty, and verification.
* [[BITwiki:Classification]] — namespaces, entity types, domains, scope, categories, and semantic relationships.
* [[BITwiki:Navigation]] — portals, indexes, graphs, and discovery.
* [[BITwiki:Glossary]] — core terminology.

